/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = ("<div class=\"getting-started-accordion\" *ngIf=\"hasEnablementContent\">\n  <p-accordion>\n    <p-accordionTab [selected]=\"shouldShow\" class=\"ld-body-large\">\n      <p-header>\n        Node Updates in <em>v1.592</em>\n      </p-header>\n\n      <ng-container *ngFor=\"let ref of selectorTemplateRefs\">\n        <div class=\"accordion-content\">\n          <ng-container *ngTemplateOutlet=\"ref\"></ng-container>\n        </div>\n      </ng-container>\n    </p-accordionTab>\n  </p-accordion>\n</div>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'setVariable'\">\n  <header><b>Store Variables in LeanData</b></header>\n  <p>\n    Store your own values (such as text, numbers, and true/false) or Objects (such as \"Matched Account\") with all of their fields in a variable (container). Use this variable to make decisions and take actions (such as assigning and merging records).\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'matchNodes'\">\n  <header><b>Set Variable for Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }}</b></header>\n  <p>\n    Store the Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} in a variable (container). Use this variable to make decisions and take actions (including assigning and merging records).\n    In most cases, users set the Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} to the <em>Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} (Default)</em> variable however, it can be set to your own {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable.\n  </p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable was set in the “{{ graphObjectType }} to {{ secondaryObjectType }} Match” node when added to the graph. With this update, you are empowered to set your own variable and reference as needed.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'actionNodes'\">\n  <header><b>{{ secondaryObjectType }} Selection</b></header>\n  <p>Now, you can choose which {{ secondaryObjectType }} (variable) you want to route the {{ sObjectType }} to.\n  <br/>In most cases, users select the <em>Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} (Default)</em> variable, however, it can be set to your own {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable.</p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable was selected when the “Route to Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }}” node was connected to the “Match” node. \n    With this update, you are empowered to set your own variable and reference as needed.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'actionNodes2'\">\n  <header><b>{{ secondaryObjectType }} Selection</b></header>\n  <p>Now, you can choose which {{ secondaryObjectType }} (variable) you want to route the {{ sObjectType }} to.\n  <br/>In most cases, users select the <em>Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} (Default)</em> variable, however, it can be set to your own {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable.</p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Matched Account variable was selected when the “Route to Matched Account” node was connected to the “Match” node. With this update, you are empowered to set your own variable and reference as needed.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'updateRecord'\">\n  <header><b>Update {{ sObjectType }} record</b></header>\n  <p>Now, you can choose to update the Routed {{ sObjectType }} record or any other related record (variable). With this added flexibility, we renamed this node to <em>Update Record</em>.</p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Routed {{ sObjectType }} variable was selected when the “Update {{ sObjectType }}” node was added to the graph.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'assignOwner'\">\n  <header><b>Assign Record</b></header>\n  <p>Now, you can choose to assign the Routed {{ sObjectType }} record or any other related record (variable). With this added flexibility, we renamed this node to <em>Assign Record</em>.</p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Routed {{ sObjectType }} variable was selected when the “Assign Owner” node was added to the graph.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'specialtyDecisionNodes'\">\n  <header><b>Select Items to Compare</b></header>\n  <p>Welcome to the new look of decision nodes.</p>\n  <p>Now, you can choose which variables to compare in your conditions for more flexibility than ever before. The Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} is selected by default, however, you can compare any {{ secondaryObjectType }} of your choice.</p>\n  <p>\n    <em>Note: Variables have always been used in LeanData. A Matched {{ secondaryObjectType }} variable was selected and compared to the Routed {{ sObjectType }} when the “Decision” node was connected to the “Match” node.</em>\n  </p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n\n<ng-template ld-dynamicTemplate [tName]=\"'generalDecisionNodes'\">\n  <header><b>Select Items to Compare</b></header>\n  <p>Welcome to the new look of decision nodes.</p>\n  <p>Choose which items (variables or values) to compare in your conditions for more flexibility than ever before.</p>\n  <p class=\"learn-more-about-variables\"><a target=\"_blank\" href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\">Learn more about Variables</a></p>\n</ng-template>\n");

