/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = ("<div class=\"modal-cont\">\n  <div class=\"middle\">\n\n    <div class=\"middle-content\">\n      <div class=\"modal-message ld-body-large\">\n        Variables are containers that store information to use in your routing logic. Use variables to make decisions and take actions (including assigning and merging records). Variables are differentiated by their <em>Data Type</em>, which store different types of information.\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"cont\">\n        <div class=\"left\">\n          <div class=\"ld-section-header-small\">Variable Data Types Supported in this Node</div>\n          <div *ngIf=\"mode === 'AllTypes'; else otherTable\">\n            <div class=\"vem-table\">\n              <div class=\"vem-header\">\n                <div class=\"data-type-col\">Data Type</div>\n                <div class=\"defn-col\">Definition</div>\n              </div>\n              <div class=\"vem-rows\">\n                <div class=\"vem-row\">\n                  <div class=\"data-type-col\">\n                    Object\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"defn-col\">\n                    Stores a record and all of its field values\n\n                    <div class=\"subtext\">\n                      <em>Example:</em> Store a Matched Account. Then, reference any Account field, such as ‘Account Owner’,\n                      later in the path\n                    </div>\n\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"vem-row\">\n                  <div class=\"data-type-col\">\n                    Text\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"defn-col\">\n                    Stores IDs, descriptions, text, or data from a field\n\n                    <div class=\"subtext\">\n                      <em>Example:</em> Store text such as account ID, then reference it in a ‘Decision’ node later in the path\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"vem-row\">\n                  <div class=\"data-type-col\">\n                    Number\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"defn-col\">\n                    Stores a numeric value from a field\n\n                    <div class=\"subtext\">\n                      <em>Example:</em> Store an Opportunity’s Amount, then reference it in a ‘Decision’ node later in the path\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n                <div class=\"vem-row\">\n                  <div class=\"data-type-col\">\n                    True/False\n                  </div>\n                  <div class=\"defn-col\">\n                    Stores a true/false value\n\n                    <div class=\"subtext\">\n                      <em>Example:</em> Store a value such as whether a checkbox was selected\n                    </div>\n                  </div>\n                </div>\n              </div>\n            </div>\n          </div>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"right\" [ngClass]=\"{'all-types': mode === 'AllTypes'}\">\n          <iframe width=\"460\" height=\"240\" src=\"https://www.youtube.com/embed/hlWxpZynZEM\" title=\"YouTube video player\" frameborder=\"0\" allow=\"accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture; web-share\" allowfullscreen></iframe>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n\n      <div class=\"bottom\" [ngClass]=\"{'all-types': mode === 'AllTypes'}\">\n        <div class=\"getting-started-accordion\">\n          <div class=\"ld-body-medium-bold bottom-header-text\">Sample Use Cases & Graphs</div>\n          <p-accordion\n            expandIcon=\"right-arrow-icon small-arrow-props\"\n            collapseIcon=\"down-arrow-icon small-arrow-props\"\n          >\n            <p-accordionTab\n              [selected]=\"false\"\n              class=\"ui-accordion-bold\"\n              [transitionOptions]=\"'0ms'\">\n              <p-header class=\"ld-body-medium\">\n                Basic\n              </p-header>\n              <div class=\"accordion-body\">\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\">\n                  For a basic case, use a variable for the Matched Account. The ‘Lead-to-Account Match’ node identifies and stores the <em>matched account</em> in the <strong class=\"font-semi-bold\">Matched Account (Default)</strong> variable. This variable can then be used downstream for decisions, routing, and more.  \n                </p>\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\" [style.margin-top.px]=\"12\">\n                  <em>Sample Graph</em><br />\n                  To download and use a sample graph, go to the <a href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ld-link\">Help Center</a> and download the\n                  <em>Basic - Route to Matched Account Graph.txt</em> file.<br />\n                  Then, import this graph template on your\n                  <a href=\"/apex/Dashboard#routing/flowbuilder/graphs/lead\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ld-link\">Lead FlowBuilder Page</a> to view (or copy) this\n                  basic use case.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n            </p-accordionTab>\n\n            <p-accordionTab\n              [selected]=\"false\"\n              class=\"ui-accordion-bold\"\n              [transitionOptions]=\"'0ms'\">\n              <p-header class=\"ld-body-medium\">\n                Advanced\n              </p-header>\n              <div class=\"accordion-body\">\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\">\n                  An advanced use case of variables is setting your own variable. \n                </p>\n\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\" [style.margin-top.px]=\"15\">\n                  Example 1:\n                  Create a custom variable to identify different types of Matched Accounts. Use one Match node to identify Matched Accounts in EMEA and another for APAC. Then, use the two variables to make decisions and route accordingly to the appropriate Matched Account.   \n                </p>\n\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\" [style.margin-top.px]=\"15\">\n                  Example 2:\n                  Set your own variable to commonly used values such as email domains to exclude (domain 1, domain 2, etc.). Use this variable in desired locations across your graph to prevent duplicative input of information. \n                </p>\n\n                <p class=\"ld-body-medium\" [style.margin-top.px]=\"15\">\n                  <em>Sample Graph</em><br />\n                  To download and use a sample graph, go to the <a href=\"https://leandatahelp.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/7237075826459-Routing-Using-Variables-in-Routing\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ld-link\">Help Center</a> and download the\n                  <em>Advanced - Route to Matched Int'l Account Graph.txt</em> file.<br />\n                  Then, import this graph template on your\n                  <a href=\"/apex/Dashboard#routing/flowbuilder/graphs/lead\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"ld-link\">Lead FlowBuilder Page</a> to view (or copy) this\n                  basic use case.\n                </p>\n              </div>\n            </p-accordionTab>\n          </p-accordion>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"spacer\"></div>\n  </div>\n\n  <div class=\"hr\"></div>\n\n  <div class=\"buttons-container\">\n    <div class=\"ld-secondary-large-button\" (click)=\"onClose()\">Close</div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n\n<ng-template #otherTable>\n  <div class=\"vem-table\">\n    <div class=\"vem-header\">\n      <div class=\"data-type-col\">Data Type</div>\n      <div class=\"defn-col\">Definition</div>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"vem-rows\">\n      <div class=\"vem-row\">\n        <div class=\"data-type-col\">\n          Object\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"defn-col\">\n          Stores a record and all of its field values\n\n          <div class=\"subtext\">\n            <em>Example:</em> Store a Matched Account. Then, reference any Account field, such as ‘Account Owner’,\n            later in the path\n          </div>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</ng-template>\n");

