/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = ("<div id=\"sendoso-wrapper\" class=\"angular-page-wrapper-props ld-body-medium\">\n  <ld-breadcrumbs [breadcrumbs]=\"breadcrumbs\"></ld-breadcrumbs>\n\n\n  <div class=\"ld-header\">Integrations</div>\n\n  <div class=\"partner-config-header-section with-separator\">\n    <div class=\"sendoso-icon partner-icon-prop\"></div>\n    <div class=\"partner-config-header-description-wrapper ld-body-large\">\n      <div class=\"ld-subheader\">\n        {{ partnerLabel }}\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-body-large\">\n        {{ summary }}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  \n  <div class=\"partner-config-body-section\">\n    <div class=\"partner-instructions-section\">\n      <div class=\"ld-section-header get-started-header\">\n        Recommended for:\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-body-large get-started-description extra-margin\">\n        <ul>\n          <li>Leads/Contacts who have gone above &amp; beyond to work with you</li>\n          <ul>\n            <li>High fit, highly engaged personas from recent Campaigns</li>\n            <li>High fit job titles and levels from target accounts</li>\n            <li>Previous customers who have changed jobs</li>\n            <li>Existing customers who have recently renewed or expanded their usage</li>\n            <li>Champions in a recently closed, high ACV sales opportunity</li>\n          </ul>\n          <li>Marketing/Sales teams manually assessing gift recipients from marketing automation/Salesforce data</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-header\">\n        Plays:\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper extra-margin\">\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>Send a gift to high fit persona from a recent campaign on behalf of Sales</li>\n            <li>Automate an outbound gift campaign to key personas from strategic accounts on behalf of Sales</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper\">\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">\n          Play #1\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">Automatically send a gift to high fit personas from a recent campaign on behalf of Sales</div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large italic instructions-subheader\">\n          Implementation Steps [Lead and Contact Routing]\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>In Sendoso, navigate to the Touches tab and configure a Salesforce Triggered Touch based on Lead/Contact field update(s) for your desired campaign's follow-up gift.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>LeanData will populate these fields to fire Sendoso. For example, updating a 'Fire Sendoso' custom field to true, or updating a text field with the gifting reason. For detailed implementation information on the Salesforce Triggered Touch in Sendoso, see <a href=\"https://sendoso.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360000104012-Setting-up-a-Salesforce-Triggered-Touch\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <li>In LeanData Lead/Contact FlowBuilder, trigger Routing by configuring the Updated Campaign Member Trigger for engaged prospects from your recent virtual event, tradeshow, or webinar.</li>\n            <li>Ensure the record proceeds through your routing process to the appropriate sales rep based on your sales strategy.</li>\n            <li>Once routed, assess whether the contact qualifies for your gift criteria by checking the persona attributes or other data points via a decision node.</li>\n            <li>If the contact qualifies, connect the decision node to a Sendoso node.</li>\n            <li>Connect and configure the Sendoso node in LeanData to update the field corresponding to the appropriate Triggered Touch condition from Step #1.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper\">\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">\n          Play #2\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">Automate an outbound gift campaign to key personas from strategic accounts on behalf of Sales</div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large italic instructions-subheader\">\n          Implementation Steps [Lead and Contact Routing]\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>In Sendoso, navigate to the Touches tab and configure a Salesforce Triggered Touch based on Lead/Contact field update(s) for your desired campaign's follow-up gift.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>LeanData will populate these fields to fire Sendoso. For example, updating a 'Fire Sendoso' custom field to true, or updating a text field with the gifting reason. For detailed implementation information on the Salesforce Triggered Touch in Sendoso, see <a href=\"https://sendoso.zendesk.com/hc/en-us/articles/360000104012-Setting-up-a-Salesforce-Triggered-Touch\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <li>In LeanData Lead/Contact FlowBuilder, use Lead to Account matching to check if the Account is a strategic account or target account to include in this campaign.</li>\n            <li>Ensure the record proceeds through your routing process to the appropriate sales rep based on your sales strategy. </li>\n            <li>Once routed, assess whether the contact qualifies for your gift criteria by checking the persona attributes or other data points via a decision node.</li>\n            <li>If the contact qualifies, connect the decision node to a Sendoso node.</li>\n            <li>Connect and configure the Sendoso node in LeanData to update the field corresponding to the appropriate Triggered Touch condition from Step #1.</li>\n            <li>Configure a one-time or scheduled job via Routing Scheduler to fire this routing graph on Leads and Contacts that meet your qualification criteria for this outbound campaign.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n");

