/* harmony default export */ __webpack_exports__["default"] = ("<div id=\"sixsense-intent-wrapper\" class=\"angular-page-wrapper-props ld-body-medium\">\n  <ld-breadcrumbs [breadcrumbs]=\"breadcrumbs\"></ld-breadcrumbs>\n\n  <div class=\"ld-header\">Integrations</div>\n\n  <div class=\"partner-config-header-section with-separator\">\n    <div class=\"sixsense-icon partner-icon-prop\"></div>\n    <div class=\"partner-config-header-description-wrapper ld-body-large\">\n      <div class=\"ld-subheader\">\n        {{ partnerLabel }}\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-body-large\">\n        {{ summary }}\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n  \n  <div class=\"partner-config-body-section\">\n    <div class=\"partner-instructions-section\">\n      <div class=\"ld-section-header get-started-header\">\n        Recommended for:\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-body-large get-started-description extra-margin\">\n        <ul>\n          <li>Sales reps aligned to a territory model</li>\n          <li>Sales reps manually prioritizing accounts in the book of business</li>\n          <li>Large volume of unassigned accounts in Salesforce</li>\n        </ul>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-header\">\n        Plays:\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper extra-margin\">\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>Notify Reps when an account spikes in intent</li>\n            <li>Ensure Reps follow up on high intent Accounts</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper\">\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">\n          Play #1\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">Notify reps when an account spikes in intent</div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large italic instructions-subheader\">\n          Implementation Steps [Account Routing]\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>In LeanData Account FlowBuilder, configure the 6sense Updated Trigger to activate when an account spikes in intent per your 6sense data model.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>Typically, this happens when an account meets your 6QA definition or reaches a Buying Stage of Decision or Purchase.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <li>Use decision nodes to check if the account's current owner is active &amp; valid per your organization's sales strategy.</li>\n            <li>If the account's owner is active, simply notify them of the spike in intent through the preferred communications channel, such as Slack or Microsoft Teams.</li>\n            <li>If the account's owner is active, simply notify them of the spike in intent through the preferred communications channel, such as Slack or Microsoft Teams.</li>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n      <div class=\"instruction-wrapper\">\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">\n          Play #2\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-section-header instructions-subheader\">Ensure reps follow up on high intent accounts</div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large italic instructions-subheader\">\n          Implementation Steps [Account Routing]\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"ld-body-large instructions-content\">\n          <ol>\n            <li>After ensuring the account has a valid sales rep following up from Play #1, connect a Hold Until node.</li>\n            <li>Configure the desired time frame for your SLA in the Hold Until based on your definition of priority for this account's follow-up.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>A sample expectation is for a repto follow up within 5 business days after the account reached a buying stage of Decision or Purchase.</li>\n            </ol>\n            <li>Configure your success exit conditions based on your definition of a qualifying sales rep follow-up.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>This can include field changes on the Account, or activity creation on the Account, such as via a Sales Engagement tool (Outreach, Salesloft, Sales Engagement).</li>\n            </ol>\n            <li>Configure your 'Time Expired' condition to take action when your rep misses an SLA.</li>\n            <ol type=\"a\">\n              <li>This can include a warning notification to the rep, escalation to sales management to ensure accountability, or re-routing to another available rep to ensure the potential opportunity is not missed.</li>\n            </ol>\n          </ol>\n        </div>\n      </div>\n    </div>\n  </div>\n</div>\n");

