/**
 * How the Match Settings work:
 * There are four options
 * 1: All LeanData matches
 * 2: All exact email matches
 * 3: Exact email matches that are also LeanData matches
 * 4: Exact email matches plus LeanData matches
 *
 * These options control these two boolean settings
 * 1: email matches are dupes (isEmailMatchDupes)
 * 2: only email matches are dupes (emailMergePreference)
 *
 * Setting 1 makes all email matches be considered duplicates
 * Setting 2 makes only email matches be considered duplicates
 *
 * Option 1 will set settings 1 and 2 to false, so only LeanData matching is used
 * Option 2 will set 1 and 2 to true, so all email matches are used (1=true) and leandata matches are excluded (2=true)
 * Option 3 will set 1 to false and 2 to true, so that only leandata matches will be considered duplicates (1=false),
 * but they will require the email match as well (2=true)
 * Option 4 will set 1 to true and 2 to false, so that all email matches are considered duplicates (1=true),
 * and leandata matches are also detected (2=false)
 */


